# {{.Name}}

CNB build pipeline: config, materials, and Dockerfiles.

## Layout

| Path | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `pipeline.toml` | stages, placeholders, static checks |
| `assets.toml` | third-party materials (version, url, unpack rules) |
| `docker/base.dockerfile` | base image for every stage |
| `docker/builder.dockerfile` | lifecycle + buildpacks on top of the base |

## Usage

```bash
just lock lifecycle    # download materials, write assets.lock.toml
just sync              # unpack into the bundle
just check             # validate config and materials
just plan              # print the resolved commands
just lint              # check Dockerfile COPY sources (after sync)
just build             # run the pipeline
```

`CNB_BIN` overrides the `cnb` binary (default: `cnb` from `PATH`).

## Notes

- Base image: `[spec.project.base]` in `pipeline.toml`
- Container CLI: first token of each stage in `run` (`podman` by default)
- The builder image runs as non-root user `cnb` (uid/gid 1000); `/layers`,
  `/workspace`, `/platform` are writable for that user
- Placeholders use full config paths (`${spec.project.platform}`); run
  `just vars` to see resolved values.
